From: Undisputed Seraphim <undisputed.seraphim@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: 8814a: program the band on the first channel set

rtw8814a_set_channel() only calls rtw8814a_switch_band() when the band
read back from REG_CCK_CHECK differs from the band of the new channel.
The chip powers up in 2G mode (CCK_CHECK clear) but with the per-band RFE
registers never written, so a module whose first channel is a 2.4 GHz one
never runs the 2G branch: the RFE pinmux and the ANTSW/ANTSWB LNA control
stay at the 5 GHz default values (0x54775477, INVSEL 0x54) instead of the
2G ones (0x72707270, INVSEL 0x72), and TXPSEL/CCK_RX/RXPSEL are not set
either.  A module that starts on 5 GHz is unaffected because 2G -> 5G is
a band change and does take the switch.

On an AP5100W this left the 2.4 GHz front end ~60 dB down in both
directions (beacon -65 dBm instead of -4 dBm at 0.5 m, RX about -90 dBm),
while 5 GHz worked.

Track the band actually programmed into the chip and take the band switch
when it does not match, so the first set_channel() always programs the
band.  Doing it here rather than from power_on() matters: at power-on the
efuse has not been read yet, so the RFE registers would get the option-0
values and the first set_channel() would again see no band change.
rtw88xxa_power_on() already does an unconditional switch_band(2G); the
8814A simply never got the equivalent.

Signed-off-by: Undisputed Seraphim <undisputed.seraphim@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.h
@@ -1978,6 +1978,10 @@
 	u8 current_primary_channel_index;
 	u8 current_band_width;
 	u8 current_band_type;
+	/* band whose RFE pins and CCK/OFDM path are programmed into the
+	 * chip; 0 means "not programmed yet"
+	 */
+	u8 programmed_band_type;
 	u8 primary_channel;
 
 	/* center channel for different available bandwidth,
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8814a.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8814a.c
@@ -225,6 +225,12 @@
 		rtw_write32_mask(rtwdev, 0x1994, 0xf, 0xf);
 		rtw_write8_set(rtwdev, REG_GPIO_MUXCFG + 2, 0xc0);
 	}
+
+	/* The chip comes up in 2G mode with the per-band RFE registers never
+	 * written, so make the next set_channel() program the band even if
+	 * the band it detects does not change.
+	 */
+	rtwdev->hal.programmed_band_type = 0;
 }
 
 #define RTW_TXSCALE_SIZE 37
@@ -1167,8 +1173,11 @@
 	else
 		new_band = RTW_BAND_2G;
 
-	if (new_band != old_band)
+	if (new_band != old_band ||
+	    new_band != rtwdev->hal.programmed_band_type) {
 		rtw8814a_switch_band(rtwdev, new_band, bw);
+		rtwdev->hal.programmed_band_type = new_band;
+	}
 
 	rtw8814a_switch_channel(rtwdev, channel);
 
